! Step 12 hand-back

Head `03960c0343e5cb4d7d3e0c53bb178d85b175ca5d`; worktree clean; no live seats; no push. Requests 017–020 received receipts; next request 021. Both commits carry the supplied attribution trailers.

* `c33b52e66` commits the aside/lift red with the unchanged-aside control. Relay 017: 28 pass, 1 fail, the same grant remains unseated after a lift and daemon change.
* `03960c034` retains aside refusals without memoizing them and marks the seat for retry on daemon changes; it also independently refuses an aside even if the supplied verifier accepts. Relay 019: 30 pass, 0 fail. Other final refusals still memoize. Retries with aside never ingest; a later clear standing can ingest the same grant.
* Important limitation: the tests directly call `daemonChanged`; production subscribes to daemon-bag changes at `operator-daemon-behavior.ts:1540`, while the standing reader reads the fleet board. Whether a fleet-board lift itself reaches that subscription remains unverified; trace and wire a real board-change wake with a caller-level red and control. The stale boot-time KEL snapshot and final fork memoization likewise remain owed. This step does not establish full live lift recovery.

Still owed: all other slice 2 rows in state, including tri-state ring, founder lineage freshness/rollback, epoch-free consumers and test hygiene, join wiring and TOCTOU, independently evidenced complete-view known-dyad census, runApplyAdmitPayload, holder-session-proof, and leaf-peer-proof. The edge board has no roster or completeness proof (`kapae.mem` #/four-edges); never infer fleet completeness from it. Whole non-daemon suites remain due before ready; e2e stays in CI. Blind Opus custody read precedes land; no push without controller go. The roll guard and epoch fields remain intact.

Next: trace and test the actual fleet-board lift wake, and continue the remaining rows red-first with controls. Keep step counter at 12 per step law.

